her than the plane? To take the easiest open example: (https://www.combinatorics.org/files/Surveys/ds21/ds21v4-2020.pdf)\nciteturn0search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6.7 years ago; For most, it is either an immediate consequence (pair crossing number, local crossing number) or irrelevant (bipartite and book crossing number, for example). ... *ArXiv e-prints*, July 2016. arXiv:1607.00131 (last accessed 9/21/2017).\n\n**Question 8.** Is there a function \\(f\\) so that \\(cr(G) \\le f(\\widetilde{cr}(G))\\) for all graphs \\(G\\)?\n\n**Acknowledgments**\n\nThanks to Markus Chimani, Jan Kynčl, Gelasio Salazar and Paul Kainen for corrections and comments, Heiko Harborth for supplying me with many sources which I had missed, and the anonymous referees for many helpful suggestions. Finally, thanks are due to the DePaul librarians who have tracked down many papers for me which are not available online.\n\n**References**\n\n[1] Bernardo M. Ábrego, Oswin Aichholzer, Silvia Fernández-Merchant, Pedro Ramos, and Gelasio Salazar. The 2-Page Crossing Number of \\(K_n\\). *Discrete Comput. Geom.*, 49(4):747–777, 2013. 35\n\n[2] Bernardo M. Ábrego, Oswin Aichholzer, Silvia Fernández-Merchant, Pedro Ramos, and Gelasio Salazar. More on the crossing number of \\(K_n\\): Monotone drawings. *Electronic Notes in Discrete Mathematics*, 44(0):411–414, 2013. 65\n\n[3] Bernardo M. Ábrego, Oswin Aichholzer, Silvia Fernández-Merchant, Pedro Ramos, and Gelasio Salazar. Shellable drawings and the cylindrical crossing number of \\(K_n\\). *Discrete Comput. Geom.*, 52(4):743–753, 2014. 35, 44, 65\n\n[4] Bernardo M. Ábrego, Mario Cetina, Silvia Fernández-Merchant, Jesús Leaños, and Gelasio Salazar. On \\(\\le k\\)-edges, crossings, and halving lines of geometric drawings of \\(K_n\\). *Discrete Comput. Geom.*, 48(1):192–215, 2012. 68, 70\n\n[5] Bernardo M. Ábrego, Julia Dandurand, Silvia Fernández-Merchant, Evgeniya Lagoda, and Yakov Sapozhnikov. Book crossing numbers of the complete graph and small local convex crossing numbers. *ArXiv e-prints*, July 2016. arXiv:1607.00131 (last accessed 9/21/2017). 35\n\nTHE ELECTRONIC JOURNAL OF COMBINATORICS (2020), #DS21 81--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nau:Dandurand_J in:math - SciRate Search (https://scirate.com/search?q=au%3ADandurand_J+in%3Amath)\nciteturn0search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 10.4 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; ~Ábrego and Julia Dandurand and Silvia Fernández-Merchant and Evgeniya Lagoda and Yakov Sapozhnikov}, title = {{B}ook crossing numbers of the complete graph and small local convex crossing numbers}, year = {2016}, eprint = {1607.00131}, note = {arXiv:1607.00131v3} }[Button: Copy Citation] ... Our proofs rely on bounding the number of edges in convex graphs with small local crossing numbers.\n\n1 results for au:Dandurand_J in:math\n\nShow all abstracts\n\n  * Book crossing numbers of the complete graph and small local convex crossing numbers\n\nBernardo M. Ábrego, Julia Dandurand, Silvia Fernández-Merchant, Evgeniya Lagoda, Yakov Sapozhnikov\n\nJul 04 2016 math.CO arXiv:1607.00131v3\n\n[Button: Scited][Button: Scite!]\n\n0\n\n@misc{1607.00131, author = {Bernardo M.~Ábrego and Julia Dandurand and Silvia Fernández-Merchant and Evgeniya Lagoda and Yakov Sapozhnikov}, title = {{B}ook crossing numbers of the complete graph and small local convex crossing numbers}, year = {2016}, eprint = {1607.00131}, note = {arXiv:1607.00131v3} }[Button: Copy Citation]\n\nPDF\n\nA $ k $-page book drawing of a graph $ G $ is a drawing of $ G $ on $ k $ halfplanes with common boundary $ l $, a line, where the vertices are on $ l $ and the edges cannot cross $ l $. The $ k $-page book crossing number of the graph $ G $, denoted by $ \\nu_k(G) $, is the minimum number of edge-crossings over all $ k $-page book drawings of $ G $. Let $G=K_n$ be the complete graph on $n$ vertices. We improve the lower bounds on $ \\nu_k(K_n) $ for all $ k\\geq 14 $ and determine $ \\nu_k(K_n) $ whenever $ 2 < n/k \\leq 3 $. Our proofs rely on bounding the number of edges in convex graphs with small local crossing numbers. In particular, we determine the maximum number of edges that a convex graph with local crossing number at most $ \\ell $ can have for $ \\ell\\leq 4 $.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nΑποτελέσματα αναζήτησης - \"Lagoda, Evgeniya\" :: Library Catalog (https://vufind2.lib.aegean.gr/EDS/Search?lookfor=%22Lagoda%2C+Evgeniya%22&type=AU)\nciteturn0search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; ## Book crossing numbers of the complete graph and small local convex crossing numbers ... Σύνδεσμος πρόσβασης: http://arxiv.org/abs/1607.00131 ... ## On the Crossing Number of 2-Page Book Drawings of Kn\\documentclass[12pt]{minimal} \\usepackage{amsmath} \\usepackage{wasysym} \\usepackage{amsfonts} \\usepackage{amssymb} \\usepackage{amsbsy} \\usepackage{mathrsfs} \\usepackage{upgreek} \\setlength{\\oddsidemargin}{-69pt} \\begin{document}$$K_{n}$$\\end{document} with Prescribed Number of Edges in Each Page\n## k-regular maps and cohomology theory of configuration spaces\n\nΣυγγραφείς: Lagoda, Evgeniya\n\nΠηγή: Lagoda, Evgeniya: k-regular maps and cohomology theory of configuration spaces, Berlin: Freie Universität Berlin 2025.\n\nΘεματικοί όροι: Mathematik\n\nΠεριγραφή αρχείου: image/jpeg; application/pdf\n\nΔιαθεσιμότητα: https://digital.zlb.de/viewer/resolver?urn=urn:nbn:de:kobv:188-refubium-47773-4\n\nView record from BASE\n\n## Book crossing numbers of the complete graph and small local convex crossing numbers\n\nΣυγγραφείς: Ábrego, Bernardo M., Dandurand, Julia, Fernández-Merchant, Silvia, Lagoda, Evgeniya, Sapozhnikov, Yakov\n\nΘεματικοί όροι: Mathematics - Combinatorics, 05C10, 05C62, 52C10, 68R10\n\nΣύνδεσμος πρόσβασης: http://arxiv.org/abs/1607.00131\n\nView this record from Arxiv\n\n## On the Crossing Number of 2-Page Book Drawings of Kn\\documentclass[12pt]{minimal} \\usepackage{a